# nano's interrupt tie-off, declared in every riscv-formal harness in nano/formal/; format and rationale in docs/manifests/interrupt-tie-off.md.
# There is no MULTIHART_TIE_OFF beside it: nano is one hart with no arbiter, and docs/manifests/interrupt-tie-off.md says why that needs no manifest.

HARNESS  wrapper.v
HARNESS  complete.sv
HARNESS  dmemcheck.sv
HARNESS  imemcheck.sv
HARNESS  ill_e.sv

# The one harness that leaves irq_meip free: the oracle for trap entry and the interrupt path.
FREE     traps.sv

UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_channel.sv
UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_macros.vh
UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_insn_check.sv
UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_ill_check.sv
UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_fault_check.sv
UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv
UPSTREAM checks/rvfi_pc_bwd_check.sv
